title: Election of the Supreme Chancellor
subtitle: The Senate chooses who will lead the Republic.
tags: event
priority: -2
view-if: not finale and not game_ending and not election_suspended and (election_due = 1 or (next_election_date > 0 and date >= next_election_date))
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_senate.svg
on-arrival: {!
SW.rotateRcLeader(Q);
SW.senateSession(Q);
SW.electionOpen(Q);
!}

= Election of the Supreme Chancellor

[? if valorum_fallen and elections_held = 0 : With Valorum brought down, the Senate must choose a new Supreme Chancellor. ?][? if govt_fell_now : The government of Chancellor [+ el_incumbent +] has fallen. [? if fall_reason = "collapse" : The [+ walkout_name +] walked out of the coalition and brought it down. ?][? if fall_reason = "bureaucrats" : A crisis manufactured by the Senate bureaucracy brought it down. ?][? if fall_reason = "vonc" : The Senate withdrew its confidence. ?][? if fall_reason = "budget" : The Senate rejected its budget twice in a row. ?][? if fall_reason = "withdrew" : The Caucus withdrew its support. ?][? if fall_reason = "confidence" : The Senate voted down the Chancellor's call for a fresh mandate. ?] The Senate must choose who will lead the Republic for the next four years. ?][? if not govt_fell_now and (elections_held > 0 or not valorum_fallen) : Supreme Chancellor [+ el_incumbent +]'s term has run its course, and the Senate must choose who will lead the Republic for the next four years. ?] Each bloc will back the candidate it trusts most. If no one wins a majority on the first ballot, the two leading candidates go to a second.

[+ el_text +]

[? if el_warchest : **Money in the race.** [+ el_warchest_text +] ?]

[? if el_mom_note : [+ el_mom_text +] ?]

[? if naboo_sympathy and el_has_pal : The Senate is moved by the plight of Naboo, and Senator Palpatine is widely seen as the sympathetic candidate. ?]

*Each candidate has strengths with some blocs and weaknesses with others, and the Caucus's momentum sways every bloc.*

- @el_run: Run a Caucus candidate for Supreme Chancellor.
- @el_back_mod: Endorse [+ mod_leader +] of the Core Moderates.
- @el_back_rim: Endorse [+ rim_leader +] of the Rimward Coalition.
- @el_back_sec: Endorse [+ el_sec_leader +] of the Security Bloc.
- @el_back_pal: Endorse Senator Palpatine.

@el_run
view-if: el_has_rc
subtitle: Our own candidate. We will need allies from other blocs to win.
on-arrival: {! SW.elBack(Q, 'rc'); if (Q.el_nominees < 2) SW.nominate(Q, Q.el_nominee_default); !}
go-to: el_nominate if el_nominees >= 2; el_campaign if el_nominees < 2

@el_nominate
new-page: true

= Our Nominee

Who will carry the Caucus's banner? Each of our leading figures appeals to different blocs. Whoever we choose will lead the Caucus whether they win or lose.

- @nom_antilles: Bail Antilles of Alderaan.
- @nom_organa: Bail Organa of Alderaan.
- @nom_mothma: Mon Mothma of Chandrila.
- @nom_amidala: Padmé Amidala of Naboo.
- @nom_bel_iblis: Garm Bel Iblis of Corellia.

@nom_antilles
view-if: nom_ok_antilles
subtitle: [+ nom_sub_antilles +]
on-arrival: {! SW.nominate(Q, 'antilles'); !}
go-to: el_campaign

@nom_organa
view-if: nom_ok_organa
subtitle: [+ nom_sub_organa +]
on-arrival: {! SW.nominate(Q, 'organa'); !}
go-to: el_campaign

@nom_mothma
view-if: nom_ok_mothma
subtitle: [+ nom_sub_mothma +]
on-arrival: {! SW.nominate(Q, 'mothma'); !}
go-to: el_campaign

@nom_amidala
view-if: nom_ok_amidala
subtitle: [+ nom_sub_amidala +]
on-arrival: {! SW.nominate(Q, 'amidala'); !}
go-to: el_campaign

@nom_bel_iblis
view-if: nom_ok_bel_iblis
subtitle: [+ nom_sub_bel_iblis +]
on-arrival: {! SW.nominate(Q, 'bel_iblis'); !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_back_mod
view-if: el_has_mod
subtitle: Keep the Core establishment in power, and earn its gratitude.
on-arrival: {! SW.elBack(Q, 'mod'); Q.mod_relation += 5; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_back_rim
view-if: el_has_rim
subtitle: A Rim Chancellor would be a revolution. The Core will not like it.
on-arrival: {! SW.elBack(Q, 'rim'); Q.rim_relation += 6; Q.rimward_dissent -= 5; Q.inst_dissent += 4; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_back_sec
view-if: el_has_sec
subtitle: The Hawks will approve; the Pacifists will not.
on-arrival: {! SW.elBack(Q, 'sec'); Q.sec_relation += 6; Q.hawk_dissent -= 5; Q.pacifist_dissent += 8; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_back_pal
view-if: el_has_pal
subtitle: [? if evidence < 3 : He seems a decent, sensible man. ?][? if evidence >= 3 : We have heard things about Palpatine that make this very hard to justify. ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.elBack(Q, 'pal'); Q.pal_relation += 8; Q.faith -= 1; if (Q.evidence >= 3) { Q.inst_dissent += 2; Q.pacifist_dissent += 4; } !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_campaign
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.el_whip = SW.whipText(Q, Q.el_cands, Q.el_backing, '_r'); Q.el_backing_name = SW.candidateName(Q, Q.el_backing); !}

= The Campaign

The Caucus is backing **[+ el_backing_name +]**. Before the Senate votes, we can court other blocs with political capital, or win them with promises. We have [+ capital +] political capital.

[+ el_whip +]

*A pledge wins a bloc's votes outright, but it binds the Caucus until the next Chancellor election. Break it and that bloc's leader will remember.*

- @el_court_mod: Court the Core Moderates.
- @el_court_ind: Court the Independents.
- @el_court_rim: Court the Rimward Coalition.
- @el_court_sec: Court the Security Bloc.
- @el_court_guild: Court the Commerce Guilds.
- @el_pledge: Make a policy pledge.
- @el_expose: Expose the money behind Palpatine.
- @el_attack_pal: Attack Palpatine's record.
- @el_tally: Call the vote.

@el_pledge
view-if: el_pledges_made < 2
subtitle: [? if el_pledges_made = 0 : Up to two pledges per election. ?][? if el_pledges_made = 1 : One more pledge at most. ?]

= A Policy Pledge

Which promise will the Caucus make? Each one wins over a bloc, and each one ties our hands for the next four years.

- @pl_no_tariffs: Promise the guilds no trade-route tariffs.
- @pl_no_levy: Promise the Moderates no levy on the Core.
- @pl_rim_relief: Promise the Rim relief in every budget.
- @pl_defence: Promise the Security Bloc defence spending in every budget.
- @pl_no_powers: Promise the Independents no new emergency powers.
- @el_campaign: Make no promise.

@pl_no_tariffs
view-if: plo_no_tariffs
subtitle: The guilds will back us. Tariffs will be off the table at every budget.
on-arrival: {! SW.makePledge(Q, 'no_tariffs', '', 12); Q.el_pledges_made += 1; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@pl_no_levy
view-if: plo_no_levy
subtitle: The Moderates will back us. The Core levy will be off the table at every budget.
on-arrival: {! SW.makePledge(Q, 'no_levy', '', 12); Q.el_pledges_made += 1; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@pl_rim_relief
view-if: plo_rim_relief
subtitle: The Rim will back us. Every budget we support must fund relief, which is not cheap.
on-arrival: {! SW.makePledge(Q, 'rim_relief', '', 12); Q.el_pledges_made += 1; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@pl_defence
view-if: plo_defence
subtitle: The Security Bloc will back us. Every budget we support must fund the fleet. The Pacifists will grumble.
on-arrival: {! SW.makePledge(Q, 'defence', '', 12); Q.el_pledges_made += 1; Q.pacifist_dissent += 2; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@pl_no_powers
view-if: plo_no_powers
subtitle: The Independents will back us. The Caucus must vote against every new grant of emergency powers.
on-arrival: {! SW.makePledge(Q, 'no_powers', '', 12); Q.el_pledges_made += 1; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_expose
view-if: el_has_pal and el_backing != "pal" and el_bought_amt > 0 and not el_exposed
choose-if: evidence >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: We need stronger evidence (4 or more) to name the money.
subtitle: Name the backers buying votes for Palpatine. The purchased votes melt away.
on-arrival: {!
Q.el_exposed = 1;
var a = Q.el_bought_amt;
Q.bonus_guild_for_pal = (Q.bonus_guild_for_pal || 0) - a * 1.3; Q.bonus_ind_for_pal = (Q.bonus_ind_for_pal || 0) - a * 1.3; Q.bonus_mod_for_pal = (Q.bonus_mod_for_pal || 0) - a;
if (Q.naboo_sympathy) for (var i = 0; i < Q.parties.length; i++) Q['bonus_' + Q.parties[i] + '_for_pal'] = (Q['bonus_' + Q.parties[i] + '_for_pal'] || 0) - 6;
Q.corruption -= 1; Q.faith += 0.5; Q.pal_relation -= 12; Q.grand_plan += 2;
SW.momentum(Q, 0.5, 'exposing the money behind Palpatine');
!}

The Caucus lays out the money trail: shell companies on Muunilinst, donations routed through shipping cartels, a holding company no one can explain. The senators who had quietly been promised favours suddenly find they have not made up their minds after all. [? if naboo_sympathy : The sympathy for Naboo cools when the Senate sees who paid for it. ?]

- @el_campaign: Continue the campaign.

@el_court_mod
view-if: el_backing != "mod" and not el_courted_mod
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
subtitle: −1 political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.el_courted_mod = 1; Q['bonus_mod_for_' + Q.el_backing] = (Q['bonus_mod_for_' + Q.el_backing] || 0) + 14 + Q.mod_relation / 10; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_court_ind
view-if: not el_courted_ind
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
subtitle: −1 political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.el_courted_ind = 1; Q['bonus_ind_for_' + Q.el_backing] = (Q['bonus_ind_for_' + Q.el_backing] || 0) + 14 + Q.ind_relation / 10; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_court_rim
view-if: el_backing != "rim" and not el_courted_rim
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
subtitle: −1 political capital. Promises to the Rim make the Institutionalists nervous.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.el_courted_rim = 1; Q.inst_dissent += 2; Q['bonus_rim_for_' + Q.el_backing] = (Q['bonus_rim_for_' + Q.el_backing] || 0) + 14 + Q.rim_relation / 10; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_court_sec
view-if: el_backing != "sec" and not el_courted_sec
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Pacifists will grumble.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.el_courted_sec = 1; Q.pacifist_dissent += 3; Q['bonus_sec_for_' + Q.el_backing] = (Q['bonus_sec_for_' + Q.el_backing] || 0) + 14 + Q.sec_relation / 10; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_court_guild
view-if: not el_courted_guild
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The guilds are expensive. We need 2 political capital.
subtitle: −2 political capital. The Rimward wing will be furious.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 2; Q.el_courted_guild = 1; Q.rimward_dissent += 8; Q.guild_relation += 5; Q['bonus_guild_for_' + Q.el_backing] = (Q['bonus_guild_for_' + Q.el_backing] || 0) + 16 + Q.guild_relation / 10; !}
go-to: el_campaign

@el_attack_pal
view-if: el_has_pal and el_backing != "pal" and not el_attacked
subtitle: [? if evidence >= 5 : We have enough to make the charges stick. ?][? if evidence < 5 : Without hard evidence this could backfire badly. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.el_attacked = 1;
if (Q.evidence >= 5) {
    for (var i = 0; i < Q.parties.length; i++) Q['bonus_' + Q.parties[i] + '_for_pal'] = (Q['bonus_' + Q.parties[i] + '_for_pal'] || 0) - 12 - Q.evidence;
    Q.evidence_public += 1;
    Q.pal_relation -= 20;
    Q.el_attack_ok = 1;
} else {
    for (var j = 0; j < Q.parties.length; j++) Q['bonus_' + Q.parties[j] + '_for_pal'] = (Q['bonus_' + Q.parties[j] + '_for_pal'] || 0) + 6;
    Q.premature_accusations += 1;
    Q.pal_relation -= 20;
    Q.faith -= 1;
    Q.inst_dissent += 5;
    Q.el_attack_ok = 0;
}
!}
go-to: el_attack_result

@el_attack_result

[? if el_attack_ok : Our dossier on Palpatine's dealings with the Trade Federation's backers is damaging. Senators who were ready to vote for him begin to hesitate. ?][? if not el_attack_ok : The attack falls flat. With no real proof, it looks like a smear against a grieving senator from an invaded world, and Palpatine's dignified reply wins him sympathy. ?]

- @el_campaign: Continue the campaign.

@el_tally
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! SW.electionFirst(Q); !}
go-to: el_result_rc if el_done and el_winner = "rc"; el_result_other if el_done and el_winner != "rc"; el_between if not el_done

@el_between
new-page: true

= Between the Ballots

[+ el_result +]

No candidate has a majority. **[+ eb_a_name +]** and **[+ eb_b_name +]** go to a second ballot; everyone else is out. For an hour the corridors of the Senate Building become a marketplace.

[? if eb_ours_in : [+ eb_backing_name +] is still in the race. [? if eb_has_out : The [+ eb_out_name +], whose candidate [+ eb_out_cand +] is out, are now free to vote for whomever they like. ?] ?][? if eb_ours_out : [+ eb_backing_name +] is out. The Caucus's [+ eb_rc_seats +]% of the Senate could decide the second ballot, and both finalists know it. ?]

- @eb_court: Court the [+ eb_out_name +] for [+ eb_backing_name +].
- @eb_pledge: Promise the [+ eb_out_name +] [+ eb_pledge_name +].
- @eb_deal_a: Endorse [+ eb_a_name +], for a price.
- @eb_deal_b: Endorse [+ eb_b_name +], for a price.
- @eb_firm: [? if eb_ours_in : Stand firm. ?][? if eb_ours_out : Stay neutral and let our senators vote their consciences. ?]

@eb_court
view-if: eb_ours_in and eb_has_out
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
subtitle: −1 political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; SW.courtEliminated(Q); !}
go-to: el_second

@eb_pledge
view-if: eb_ours_in and eb_has_out and eb_pledge_ok and el_pledges_made < 2
subtitle: Their votes for our pledge. It will bind us for four years.
on-arrival: {! SW.makePledge(Q, Q.eb_pledge, Q.eb_out_main, 12); Q.el_pledges_made += 1; !}
go-to: el_second

@eb_deal_a
view-if: eb_ours_out and not eb_a_rc
subtitle: In return: the [+ eb_a_chair_name +] chair and a place in the government. [? if eb_a = "pal" : The Pacifists will be appalled. ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.kingmaker(Q, 'a'); if (Q.eb_a === 'pal') { Q.pacifist_dissent += 6; Q.inst_dissent += 3; } !}
go-to: el_second

@eb_deal_b
view-if: eb_ours_out and not eb_b_rc
subtitle: In return: the [+ eb_b_chair_name +] chair and a place in the government. [? if eb_b = "pal" : The Pacifists will be appalled. ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.kingmaker(Q, 'b'); if (Q.eb_b === 'pal') { Q.pacifist_dissent += 6; Q.inst_dissent += 3; } !}
go-to: el_second

@eb_firm
on-arrival: {! if (Q.eb_ours_out) Q.el_backing = ''; !}
go-to: el_second

@el_second
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! SW.electionSecond(Q); !}
go-to: el_result_rc if el_winner = "rc"; el_result_other if el_winner != "rc"

@el_result_rc
on-arrival: {! SW.prepareRcCoalitions(Q); Q.rc_chancellor_count = (Q.rc_chancellor_count || 0) + 1; !}
achievement: caucus_chancellor

= [+ el_winner_name +] is elected!

[+ el_result +]

The rotunda erupts. For the first time in a generation, a reformer holds the Republic's highest office. Now [+ el_winner_name +] must assemble a governing coalition.

- @el_coal_0: [+ el_opt0_label +]
- @el_coal_1: [+ el_opt1_label +]
- @el_coal_2: [+ el_opt2_label +]
- @el_coal_3: [+ el_opt3_label +]
- @el_coal_4: [+ el_opt4_label +]
- @el_coal_5: [+ el_opt5_label +]
- @el_coal_6: [+ el_opt6_label +]
- @el_coal_minority: Govern as a minority, relying on case-by-case support.

@el_coal_0
view-if: el_opt0
subtitle: [+ el_opt0_bureau +]
choose-if: el_opt0_ok
unavailable-subtitle: [+ el_opt0_why +]
on-arrival: {! SW.chooseRcCoalition(Q, 0); !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_coal_1
view-if: el_opt1
subtitle: [+ el_opt1_bureau +]
choose-if: el_opt1_ok
unavailable-subtitle: [+ el_opt1_why +]
on-arrival: {! SW.chooseRcCoalition(Q, 1); !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_coal_2
view-if: el_opt2
subtitle: [+ el_opt2_bureau +]
choose-if: el_opt2_ok
unavailable-subtitle: [+ el_opt2_why +]
on-arrival: {! SW.chooseRcCoalition(Q, 2); !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_coal_3
view-if: el_opt3
subtitle: [+ el_opt3_bureau +]
choose-if: el_opt3_ok
unavailable-subtitle: [+ el_opt3_why +]
on-arrival: {! SW.chooseRcCoalition(Q, 3); !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_coal_4
view-if: el_opt4
subtitle: [+ el_opt4_bureau +]
choose-if: el_opt4_ok
unavailable-subtitle: [+ el_opt4_why +]
on-arrival: {! SW.chooseRcCoalition(Q, 4); !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_coal_5
view-if: el_opt5
subtitle: [+ el_opt5_bureau +]
choose-if: el_opt5_ok
unavailable-subtitle: [+ el_opt5_why +]
on-arrival: {! SW.chooseRcCoalition(Q, 5); !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_coal_6
view-if: el_opt6
subtitle: [+ el_opt6_bureau +]
choose-if: el_opt6_ok
unavailable-subtitle: [+ el_opt6_why +]
on-arrival: {! SW.chooseRcCoalition(Q, 6); !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_coal_minority
subtitle: Every vote will be a struggle, and the coalition will be fragile.
on-arrival: {! SW.setGovt(Q, ['rc', 'ind'], 'Caucus Minority Government'); SW.openChairs(Q, Math.round(Q.rc_r) + 20); Q.coalition_dissent = 2; !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_result_other
on-arrival: {!
var members = SW.formCoalitionAuto(Q, Q.el_winner, false);
SW.setGovt(Q, members);
Q.el_invited = (Q.el_winner !== 'cis' && SW.affinity(Q, Q.el_winner, 'rc') >= 38 && Q.rc_r >= 5) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.el_backing === Q.el_winner) Q.el_invited = 1;
Q.el_walkout_blocks = (Q.walkout_bloc && Q.date < Q.walkout_until && (Q.govt_blocs || []).indexOf(Q.walkout_bloc) >= 0) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.el_walkout_blocks) Q.el_invited = 0;
Q.el_pal_won = Q.el_winner === 'pal' ? 1 : 0;
Q.el_join_bureau = SW.bureauReaction(SW.bureauComfort(Q, (Q.govt_blocs || []).concat(['rc'])));
if (Q.el_deal_won) { Q.el_invited = 1; Q.el_walkout_blocks = 0; }
SW.juniorPrice(Q);
SW.assignChairs(Q);
!}

= [+ el_winner_name +] is elected Supreme Chancellor

[+ el_result +]

[? if el_pal_won : Senator Palpatine of Naboo accepts the office with quiet humility, promising to "end the corruption and paralysis of the Senate". The galleries applaud. ?][? if not el_pal_won : [+ el_winner_name +] forms a government: the [+ coalition_name +]. ?]

[? if el_invited and el_deal_won : [+ el_winner_name +] keeps the bargain struck between the ballots: the Caucus is invited into the government, and the [+ el_deal_chair_name +] chair is ours if we join. ?][? if el_invited and not el_deal_won : The new Chancellor's office has invited the Caucus to join the governing coalition, with a share of the committee chairs. ?] [? if el_invited : [+ el_join_price +] ?][? if not el_invited and el_walkout_blocks : The [+ walkout_name +], who walked out on the Caucus, sit in the new government and will not have us. ?][? if not el_invited and not el_walkout_blocks : The new government does not need the Caucus, and has not asked for it. ?]

- @el_join: Join the government.
- @el_oppose: Remain in opposition.

@el_join
view-if: el_invited
subtitle: [? if el_pal_won : Palpatine's coalition gives us chairs and access, but ties our name to his. ?][? if not el_pal_won : Committee chairs, and a share of responsibility. ?] [+ el_join_bureau +] [+ el_join_price +]
on-arrival: {! SW.joinGovernment(Q); if (Q.el_pal_won) { Q.pacifist_dissent += 4; Q.pal_relation += 5; } !}
go-to: el_chairs

@el_oppose
subtitle: Freedom to criticise, but no committee chairs.
on-arrival: {! SW.assignChairs(Q); Q.rc_momentum += 0.5; !}

The Caucus will hold the new government to account from the opposition benches.

@el_chairs
new-page: true

= Committee Chairs

Every new government shares out the committee chairs afresh. The Caucus has [+ leverage +] leverage to spend, and holds [+ rc_chairs +] of the [+ chair_cap +] chairs our partners will let us have: each partner insists on at least one for itself, and chairs promised in the coalition talks are theirs. Each chair unlocks new Senate Affairs cards.

[? if pledge_count > 0 : Our pledges this term: [+ pledge_text +]. ?]

- @el_chair_rimaffairs: Outer Rim Affairs (5 leverage).
- @el_chair_finance: Finance & Commerce (10 leverage).
- @el_chair_judiciary: Judiciary & Intelligence (10 leverage).
- @el_chair_security: Security & Defence (12 leverage).
- @el_chairs_done: That will do.

@el_chair_rimaffairs
view-if: chair_rimaffairs != "rc"
choose-if: leverage >= 5 and rc_chairs < chair_cap and not chair_res_rimaffairs
unavailable-subtitle: [? if chair_res_rimaffairs : Promised to the [+ chair_res_rimaffairs_name +] in the coalition talks. ?][? if not chair_res_rimaffairs and rc_chairs >= chair_cap : Our partners will not give up another chair. ?][? if not chair_res_rimaffairs and rc_chairs < chair_cap : Not enough leverage. ?]
subtitle: Relief, piracy, slavery and Rim representation.
on-arrival: chair_rimaffairs = "rc"; leverage -= 5; rc_chairs += 1
go-to: el_chairs

@el_chair_finance
view-if: chair_finance != "rc"
choose-if: leverage >= 10 and rc_chairs < chair_cap and not chair_res_finance
unavailable-subtitle: [? if chair_res_finance : Promised to the [+ chair_res_finance_name +] in the coalition talks. ?][? if not chair_res_finance and rc_chairs >= chair_cap : Our partners will not give up another chair. ?][? if not chair_res_finance and rc_chairs < chair_cap : Not enough leverage. ?]
subtitle: Trade policy, the Banking Clan, and the treasury.
on-arrival: chair_finance = "rc"; leverage -= 10; rc_chairs += 1
go-to: el_chairs

@el_chair_judiciary
view-if: chair_judiciary != "rc"
choose-if: leverage >= 10 and rc_chairs < chair_cap and not chair_res_judiciary
unavailable-subtitle: [? if chair_res_judiciary : Promised to the [+ chair_res_judiciary_name +] in the coalition talks. ?][? if not chair_res_judiciary and rc_chairs >= chair_cap : Our partners will not give up another chair. ?][? if not chair_res_judiciary and rc_chairs < chair_cap : Not enough leverage. ?]
subtitle: Courts, investigations and intelligence. Vital for unmasking the Sith.
on-arrival: chair_judiciary = "rc"; leverage -= 10; rc_chairs += 1
go-to: el_chairs

@el_chair_security
view-if: chair_security != "rc"
choose-if: leverage >= 12 and rc_chairs < chair_cap and not chair_res_security
unavailable-subtitle: [? if chair_res_security : Promised to the [+ chair_res_security_name +] in the coalition talks. ?][? if not chair_res_security and rc_chairs >= chair_cap : Our partners will not give up another chair. ?][? if not chair_res_security and rc_chairs < chair_cap : Not enough leverage. ?]
subtitle: The Judicial Forces, defence policy and, one day, the army.
on-arrival: chair_security = "rc"; leverage -= 12; rc_chairs += 1
go-to: el_chairs

@el_chairs_done
on-arrival: {! SW.assignChairs(Q); Q.leverage = 0; !}

The committee assignments are confirmed. The new government begins its work.
